[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4707325420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120318#issuecomment-4707325420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120318","id":4707325420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGJQV7A","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T11:13:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T11:25:26Z","body":"Seems the error is in this code:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/df6235838b63dd49f448547406e339848455c140/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L4961-L4969\n\nThat should probably be moved to the block below which handles this kind of case:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/df6235838b63dd49f448547406e339848455c140/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L4970-L4983\n\nEdit: Transform3D is also in the wrong group, *it* should be in the first group as it doesn't have a subscript access operator (and will fail when run, but doesn't produce a parser error)\n\nEdit2: Fixing this would probably also include adding some testing for this to ensure correctness, that would be under `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts`, probably in `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/parser/features` and `modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/parser/errors`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4707325420/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4709160699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120318#issuecomment-4709160699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120318","id":4709160699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGLAW-w","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T14:49:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T14:49:35Z","body":"> Edit: Transform3D is also in the wrong group, _it_ should be in the first group as it doesn't have a subscript access operator (and will fail when run, but doesn't produce a parser error)\n\nNote that in `3.x` it works for Transform:\n<img width=\"593\" height=\"516\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/84004b0a-e86c-4061-8154-a505d8b1b253\" />\n\nIt might be the case the feature was lost by an oversight when rewriting stuff for `4.0`.\n\nSo an alternative is to allow subscript operator for Transform3D in `4.x` (`[0]` returning `basis.x`, `[1]` returning `basis.y`, `[2]` returning `basis.z`, `[3]` returning `origin`). But given no reports about this feature missing I'm not sure it's needed.\n\nMaking it produce a parser error seems like a simpler solution for now indeed. The feature could always be readded when actually needed/requested by the users.\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4709160699/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4709202508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120318#issuecomment-4709202508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120318","id":4709202508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGLC6TA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T14:53:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T14:53:51Z","body":"Most of these subscript operators seem to be unused given that this was not noticed for several years, but also wouldn't be too expensive to just add it to `Transform3D` for completeness, but making it a parser error first and then readded would probably be the most straight forward to ensure it doesn't become a confusing runtime error only\n\nBut the fact that this went unnoticed for years is a good indication it's a surface that would benefit from parser tests","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4709202508/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]